  "scope": "An actual 1440-instruction caller allocates its own zero row and graph context through the reviewed constructor, then passes that same returned context into the existing real shortest-path machine. The typed original finite graph derives all recovery-index conditions. A cost-congruence proof preserves every literal original shortest result field despite callback-charge differences, yielding exactly the original constant-zero-cost shortest oracle. The same physical run preserves input roots and source and includes terminal halt, with an input-only n/label-width instruction bound. Eight physical cases verify exact literal zero-cost path fields or absence, including directionality and padding. Initial graph/enumeration representations and address widths, actual kept-matrix composition and the ordered avoiding-demand scan remain explicit.",
